&lt;strong&gt;About the Oregon State Police&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
The Oregon State Police (OSP) is a multi-disciplined organization that safeguards Oregon&rsquo;s people, wildlife, and natural resources. OSP enforces traffic laws, investigates crimes, performs postmortem examinations and forensic analyses, conducts background checks, and manages law enforcement data. The agency also regulates gaming and enforces laws related to fish, wildlife, and natural resources. OSP includes more than 1,400 employees&mdash;troopers, investigators, and professional staff&mdash;delivering comprehensive public safety services to Oregon and supporting law enforcement partners statewide.&lt;/p&gt;

