&lt;h1&gt;Black Youth Suicide Prevention Coalition recruiting for Adult Advisory Council&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;SALEM, Ore. - The Black Youth Suicide Prevention Coalition is now accepting applications for the Adult Advisory Council to support youth-led suicide prevention and mental health advocacy. Adult advisors collaborate with and support the coalition&rsquo;s Youth Wellness Consultants by providing guidance, sharing resources and helping to shape culturally specific, community-based prevention efforts. Adults with lived experience, professional expertise, or strong community relationships are encouraged to apply.&amp;nbsp; Applications will close Feb. 28.&amp;nbsp;This role is voluntary.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To apply,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdolFhzdtfgt82OKPMN1zndyE0cIojX-GH_Ea_uGCxGfrKnSg/viewform?utm_medium=email&amp;amp;utm_source=govdelivery" rel="noopener" style="color: rgb(6, 66, 118); text-decoration-line: none; text-size-adjust: 100%;" target="_blank"&gt;submit an application&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;by Feb. 28, 2026.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;UPDATE:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;OSP is asking for any potential witnesses or anyone with information to contact OSP Dispatch at 800-442-2068 or dial *OSP (*677) from a mobile phone. Please reference case number SP26-035245. Investigators believe the pedestrian (Byam) was struck sometime between 9:45 p.m. on January 30, 2026, and 7:20 a.m. on January 31, 2026.&lt;/p&gt;

